             21  *
             22  *       THE MEM COMMAND ALLOWS PBASIC TO ALTER
             23  *       A BYTE OF MEMORY WHILE THE MEM FUNCTION
             24  *       ALLOWS PBASIC TO READ A BYTE OF
             25  *       MEMORY.
             26  *
             27  * CALLING SEQUENCE:
             28  *
             29  *       B @MEMY
             30  *
             31  *       EXIT TO NLIN
             32  *
             33  *
             34  *       B @MEMF
             35  *
             36  *       IN  (R2) = ADDRESS
             37  *       OUT (R2) = RESULT
             38  *       EXIT TO EVSFR$
             39  *
             40  * EXCEPTIONS AND CONDITIONS:
             41  *
             42  *       EVALUATION ERRORS
             43  *       SYNTAX ERROR
             44  *
ASM990 2.4.6     MEMF                       Sun Aug 10 23:07:34 2025 Page 0003
